   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public service law, in relation to prohibiting the attachment of wireless equipment and other like attachments to existing utility poles in certain circumstances",
    "basePrintNo": "S6687",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6687-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §119-a, Pub Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6687\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the public service law, in relation\nto prohibiting the attachment of wireless equipment and other like\nattachments to existing utility poles in certain circumstances\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo prohibit the attachment of wireless broadcast or relay equipment or\nany other like attachments to utility poles.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection one amends § 119-a of the Public Service Law to prohibit the\nattachment of wireless broadcast or relay equipment or any other like\nattachments to utility poles unless an existing easement is explicitly\namended to include wireless equipment or a new easement is written and\nfiled to allow for the attachment of wireless broadcast, relay\nequipment or any other like attachment to a utility pole.\n\nSection two provides an effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nMany New York residents are complaining about attachments being\ninstalled on existing utility poles. Residents argue that not only are\ntheir rights as property owners being violated but that the attachment\nof wireless broadcast or relay equipment or any other attachments to\nutilities poles could result in potential health problems as they are\nunaware of the levels of radiation such attachments emit. Moreover,\nmany NY residents are concerned about the effect on their property\nvalues as a result of attachments to utility poles.\n\nThis bill would require an existing easement be explicitly amended in\nwriting and then filed to include wireless equipment or a new easement\nbe written and filed to allow the attachment of wireless broadcast or\nrelay equipment or any other like attachment to a utility pole in\norder to protect property rights of New Yorkers.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the state.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
